{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context and confirmed RCA\n\nGerrit Verify run 31874837464 completed in 29m11s with macOS at 27m38s. The macOS default suite spent 20.88s in test_hook_falls_back_to_git_when_env_unset, 16.38s setting up build-provenance artifacts, 10.69s rebuilding from sdist, plus 8.98s in one blank-env build. Ubuntu repeats these builds in three Python cells. Local profiling showed the fallback exports the entire 3,019-file / 42.4MB checkout although hatch_build.py only resolves one SHA plus writes src/rebar/_build_info.py: git add costs 1.37-1.53s; python -m build costs 3.85-4.32s of a 6.04-6.38s test. A same-hook minimal package preserved the exact fallback SHA while reducing initial paired totals from 6.30/9.26s to 2.66/5.43s.\n\nThe exact -n 3 --dist worksteal selector proved that built_artifacts initializes separately on three workers: each consumer paid 6.60-6.74s setup, launching three full builds. This is a bounded contributor, not the cause of multi-minute host variation. The pre-repair selected-six serial baseline is 18.23s.\n\nLive run logs also prove a correctness prerequisite. The artifact job received GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION=9aecb53e then checked out that revision, but built with GITHUB_SHA=7d908fb from trusted main. Its probes accepted any non-null COMMIT. Exact source identity is required by ducal-statuelike-ladybird.\n\n## Ticket and OSS research\n\nNo prior rejection exists. ducal-statuelike-ladybird requires real sdist/wheel plus exact provenance behavior. square-tragic-llama explicitly accepted a self-contained minimal Git fixture while retaining the exact fallback SHA plus shallow-source control. despotic-dorsal-greatdane approved immutable artifact reuse but stopped at per-worker scope. cryptic-damp-panda identified repeated package builds as coverage-neutral residual work.\n\nFour popular active projects use this placement: pytest 68308aa has one Ubuntu package job before its broad matrix; pip f399c371 has dedicated packaging jobs outside Unix/Python tests; Poetry 92b74dc has one Ubuntu build/install smoke job outside its OS/Python matrix; Pydantic 02c5c975 has a dedicated Ubuntu distribution build outside its broad matrix. This is 4/4 consensus for one full-package integration job plus lighter behavioral probes in the broad matrix. Rebar remains stricter by retaining real isolated PEP 517 sdist-to-wheel execution through the production hook in every cell.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Freeze RED workflow plus build-hook contracts. The workflow oracle rejects GITHUB_SHA as artifact provenance, requires git rev-parse --short HEAD after the final checkout, then requires exact equality from installed wheel plus sdist. Build-hook oracles retain env SHA, preserved sdist SHA, git fallback SHA, blank-env failure.\n2. Create one shared fixture around the checkout-current hatch_build.py plus src/rebar/_build_info.py boundary. Migrate all three known whole-tree materialization forms: _clean_tree in test_build_provenance.py, _self_contained_checkout in test_attestation_signing.py, and the inline git archive plus tar extraction inside test_hook_fails_when_rebar_build_commit_empty. Re-derive completeness with a repository string sweep for git archive and tar extraction in build-semantics tests. The direct full-Rebar WheelBuilder content test is intentional and is not a fixture materializer.\n3. The fixture creates a tiny temporary Hatch package, copies the checkout production hatch_build.py, declares it as the real custom build hook, provides src/rebar/__init__.py at the production target boundary, initializes Git, then commits only that tiny tree. The production hook writes and force-includes src/rebar/_build_info.py into sdist and wheel, so preserve-existing is exercised through the real archive boundary. It keeps default PEP 517 isolation and never mocks Hatchling, Git, archive creation, or wheel inspection.\n4. Convert repeated semantics tests in test_attestation_signing.py plus test_build_provenance.py to that fixture. Retain every named assertion, the no-git helper branch, the direct full-Rebar WheelBuilder package-content test, plus the shallow-source control.\n5. Keep the existing full-Rebar replay in the shared _artifact-probe.yml workflow. This workflow serves both test.yml branch-head checkout plus gerrit-verify.yaml patchset checkout. In both lanes, compute REBAR_EXPECTED_COMMIT with git rev-parse --short HEAD after the applicable final checkout. Build with that short value. Assert exact equality for installed wheel plus install-from-sdist. Preserve every import, CLI, schema, packaging, plus vote-gating probe.\n6. Seed the exact wrong-SHA defect, a whole-tree fixture regression, plus one precedence defect. Require the respective oracle to return RED before restoration. Record focused serial and exact-xdist elapsed/setup timings against the pre-repair 18.23s selected-six serial baseline and 6.60-6.74s per-worker xdist setup baseline. These timings quantify runner-work impact but are evidence only, not a retention gate, because the RCA establishes this is a bounded contributor and host variation can dominate wall-clock.\n7. Run focused tests, workflow consumers, make lint, typecheck, plus full default/integration selectors. Push the necessary implementation immediately through Gerrit without a control-only run. Record hosted macOS plus Ubuntu durations from that treatment.\n\n## Test contract card\n\nauthoritative_contract: ducal-statuelike-ladybird requires real sdist-to-wheel provenance, exact env/git fallback behavior, blank-env failure, sdist preservation, plus exact source identity; both workflow consumers require artifact-probe to build their final checkout.\ntrigger_preconditions: each matrix cell runs the real production hook through isolated PEP 517 on the minimal package; artifact-probe has completed its branch-head or patchset checkout.\nproduction_path: copied production hatch_build.py resolves then writes and force-includes COMMIT during sdist plus wheel builds; artifact-probe builds then installs full distributions.\ntest_tier: minimal real-build probes across every current OS/Python cell plus one full-project artifact integration job per workflow lane.\nobservable_postcondition: existing semantics remain; full artifacts equal the short SHA of their final checkout.\nnegative_control: wrong nonempty SHA fails; blank env fails; no-git/no-bake remains None; shallow source remains supported.\ncollateral_invariants: no selector, assertion, isolation mode, worker, platform, Python cell, coverage, mutation, probe, runner, or vote dependency is removed.\nci_gate: focused serial/xdist tests, workflow contracts, make lint, make typecheck, Gerrit Verified, LLM-Review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every current OS/Python cell executes a real isolated sdist-to-wheel build through production hatch_build.py on the minimal fixture package.\n- [ ] The env-override probe requires the exact supplied SHA.\n- [ ] The install-from-sdist probe requires the exact preserved SHA.\n- [ ] The git-fallback probe requires the exact committed fixture SHA.\n- [ ] The blank-env probe requires a nonzero real-build exit.\n- [ ] The shared fixture replaces _clean_tree, _self_contained_checkout, and the inline blank-env git-archive materializer.\n- [ ] A repository string sweep confirms no other hook-semantics fixture archives the full Rebar checkout.\n- [ ] Both artifact workflow lanes derive the short expected SHA after their final checkout.\n- [ ] The installed full-Rebar wheel must equal the expected short SHA.\n- [ ] The installed full-Rebar sdist must equal the expected short SHA.\n- [ ] A wrong nonempty full-artifact SHA fails the workflow oracle.\n- [ ] The direct full-Rebar WheelBuilder content test remains enabled.\n- [ ] The shallow-source negative control remains enabled.\n- [ ] The OS/Python matrix remains unchanged.\n- [ ] The pytest selectors, xdist workers, coverage gate, plus mutation gate remain unchanged.\n- [ ] The artifact import, CLI, schema, plus vote-gating probes remain unchanged.\n- [ ] A precedence mutation returns the build-hook oracle to RED.\n- [ ] Focused serial and exact-xdist elapsed/setup timings are recorded against the pre-repair 18.23s serial and 6.60-6.74s per-worker setup baselines as evidence, without using timing as a pass/fail gate.\n- [ ] The first hosted treatment records macOS plus all Ubuntu job/test durations.\n- [ ] Gerrit records LLM-Review +1 before merge.\n- [ ] Gerrit records Verified +1 before merge.\n- [ ] Gerrit records zero unresolved comments before merge."}},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786788452445110001,"uuid":"6fe372f3-570b-4645-8ffc-993f7957b6e2"}